From 508bdb3d34f28a30deac2a9ae12ac5ae7aa88d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] notify+wake dedup: the tui defer window runs from
 the core-drain hold's lift

Review of PR #1652 at 76133d4520: stopping the DEFER_MAX_S window only while
the hold is on still let the first tui consumer to tick after a >600 s hold
deliver its notice, and the wake then started a second turn. Every notifier
leg that sees the hold on now stamps <root>/core-update/notifier-hold-seen
(mtime = last seen; fleet root so every profile/process shares it), and
wake_owes_after keeps deferring while the hold is on or was seen on less than
DEFER_MAX_S ago, i.e. the window runs from max(event, lift). A wake that never
lands still leaves the tui notice once the lift is DEFER_MAX_S old.

Tests: the hold > window test now runs with either leg ticking first after
the lift (tui-first fails at 76133d4520 with 1+1 turns); the cannot-land test
proves the notice waits for the post-lift window and is then delivered.
